  RealLifeEquivalentDescription: Commonly known as Angel's Trumpet for its large,
    pendulous blooms, Brugmansia has evolved clever ways to court different pollinators.
    Many varieties emit a powerful, sweet fragrance specifically at night to lure
    in moths from great distances. In contrast, certain red-hued species focus on
    visual appeal rather than scent, ditching the perfume to rely on the keen eyes
    of hummingbirds for pollination.
